---
description: Mandatory architecture, modularity, hardcoding, and visual rules for this repository
alwaysApply: true
---

`@AGENTS.md` is the canonical repository contract. Read it before editing. For any work
under `class-agent/`, also read `@class-agent/AGENTS.md`, every nearer `AGENTS.md`, the
relevant constitution sections, and the relevant documentation.

Do not start from a generic generated solution. Inspect and reuse the repository's
existing components, adapters, schemas, registries, resources, tokens, tests, and
extension points first.

- Let the Course Agent make semantic user-intent choices only among authorized tools,
  resources, registered components, skills and validated variants.
- Keep identity, authorization, validation, sandboxing, confirmations, persistence, and
  all other trust decisions in deterministic platform code.
- Put changeable values in configuration, registries, maintained resources, or design
  tokens; hardcode only intentional invariants and bounded trusted policy.
- Do not add chat keyword heuristics, arbitrary generated UI, scattered styling literals,
  parallel abstractions, speculative dependencies, or unrelated branches in large
  orchestrators. Unless explicitly requested but always with a warning that the priority is for the agent to make choices.
- Preserve the sparse monochrome editorial aesthetic and first-party semantic components.
- Treat stable contracts as migration/versioned boundaries and update every binding, test,
  fixture, and document required by the root instructions.

Keep changes focused, review the complete diff, and report actual verification rather than
assuming generated code is correct.
